WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.100
-So is this --
This is it?

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.934
You're not gonna...
say anything?

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:12.167
-Anyone's invited to speak,
but I'm okay with silence.

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:15.467
-So no icebreakers or...
-I, for one, I'm missing work,

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.000
not to mention I left Edward
home with my husband,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.267
which is basically like leaving
a 12-year-old boy alone

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.334
with a man who I love dearly,

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.067
but is also essentially
a 12-year-old.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.434
-Oh, hold up.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.634
Did you say
a 12-year-old boy named Edward?

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.334
Is it the Edward?

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.968
Just putting two and two
together here.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.133
-Are you the aunt?

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.534
-Yeah.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:38.767
Yeah, that's me.
I guess I'm the aunt.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:39.901
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:40.968
We're here
with Taylor Schilling.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.434
That was a clip
from "Dear Edward."

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.601
This is very --

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.300
It's a very beautiful show.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.667
Very challenging material.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.300
-Deals with a tragedy.
Also, very uplifting.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.634
-Yeah.
Yeah.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.234
You know, I think this show
is really a celebration

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:01.534
of the moments that we have to
start over, which, I mean, I --

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.868
I can relate to.
I feel like those --

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.701
kind of those moments
where you're like, "Okay.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:09.000
I really thought life was gonna
be going in this direction,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.567
and I thought
I was gonna land here,

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:13.167
but I kind of wake up,
and I'm over here."

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.701
And the process
of embracing reality.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.968
-You have a co-star
in this who is wonderful.

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.434
Is his name Colin O'Brien?
-Yes.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:22.934
-And he's 14 years old.
-Yes.

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.968
-And, is it --
I mean, I'm always taken when --

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.934
I mean, I'm assuming --

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.534
He seems like he knows exactly
what he's doing.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.067
-Mm-hmm.
-And as an actor...

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.667
-He does.
-...is it, like, intimidating,

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.267
at times, to be with, like,
a younger actor

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.434
who knows what they're doing
so well?

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:37.767
-I think so.
I mean, I think it's

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.334
mostly intimidating
that he knows --

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.300
he knows so intensely
what he's doing.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.601
And we -- we end,
and he pivots to, you know,

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.834
rocks or lava
or talking about the layers

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:50.400
of sediment in the planet.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.767
And then naming them and asking
if he can quiz me on them.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.968
-Yeah. Aren't you excited
about those quizzes?

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.501
-I'm like, "I have to focus."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.000
"Give me a minute."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.968
But, I mean, I knew more --

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:05.901
But I knew more about rocks
and things...

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.434
-Oh, so that's great.
-...when we were over.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:08.667
-So you came out of
this whole process

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.767
both with a wonderful show
and some rock knowledge.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.067
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.334
-Which you've always
been looking for.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.767
-I have.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.300
-Every time you're here,
I remember, you know,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.667
people always say,
"What do you guys talk about

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.334
during the commercial breaks?"
and I'm always like,

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.534
"Have you learned anything
about rocks?"

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.667
and you're always like, "No."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.200
Now I have,
thanks to Colin O'Brien.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.367
I've learned about rocks.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.801
He's a very,
very talented actor.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:32.801
He's very diligent,
very rigorous.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.300
-That's fun to be around.
-It is.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.534
-You -- I'm very jealous
of another actor

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:37.868
that you are friends with.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.200
And I think this friendship
has bloomed

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.901
since the last time I saw you.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:43.033
-You're friends with Jane Fonda.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.133
[ Cheers ]

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.567
That's really good.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:46.934
Taylor, that's really good.
-I know.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.734
I mean, I don't know how --
I don't know how.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.400
I'm very, very lucky.
Jane, uh --

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.267
I am, and Jane is -- Jane's a
real role model for everyone.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:01.901
She -- Jane has taught me,
you know,

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.100
we need to send thank-you cards.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.200
And she never --
Jane remembers everything.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.067
And for exa--
I mean, she's already,

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:14.634
with all of the things
she's doing, she sends notes,

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:17.968
you know, sharing her excitement
for my projects.

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:19.601
-[ Laughs ]
-And I'm grateful to her.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.067
I don't know.
You know.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.968
-It's really amazing when you
meet someone like Jane Fonda,

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:26.901
who, just their work alone,
would be impressive.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.133
-Yes.
-And then you also learn

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.501
how to be a better human being.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.400
You're like, "Oh, man, I must be
really dropping the ball."

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.767
[ Laughter ]
-It doesn't fully --

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.767
It doesn't fully make sense.
But I feel like, you know,

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:40.701
she's one of those people
that, inside of her sphere,

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.067
everybody's better.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.267
-You're just -- everybody takes
it up a notch.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.567
-You get a little closer
to Jane Fonda,

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:45.868
and you just are like --
-You're better.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.334
-"This is
the best version of me."

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:50.067
-Yeah, it's like some filter
on your phone but on your soul.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:52.534
-Has she met Tank?
-No, no.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:53.667
-That's for the best.
I think that's for the best.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.200
-Tank -- it's for the best.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.934
I don't know what Tank would do.
And Tank can't fly.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.667
-I think you have a very special
thing going with Jane,

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.167
and I don't think you should
bring Tank into the mix.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:02.367
-No, we don't need to.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.267
-I just feel like
this is a situation where Tank

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.667
could only make it
a little bit worse.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.000
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.667
I think you're right.
-Congratulations on the show.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:09.767
Thanks for being here.
-Thank you.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:10.901
-It's always so great
to see you.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.100
-Thank you for having me.
-Taylor Schilling.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.567
New episodes of "Dear Edward"

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.601
are available Fridays
on Apple TV+.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:17.133
We'll be right back
with Eddie Izzard.

